    "unified_principle_replicates": false,
    "note": "STRIP and Neural Cleanse are governed by DIFFERENT class properties, which UNSW-NB15 dissociates. STRIP's blind spot follows target-class ENTROPY: the low-entropy class is `normal` (the MINORITY here), and STRIP is indeed blindest on target-normal \u2014 so STRIP's governing factor is INTRINSIC and dissociates from frequency. Neural Cleanse's reachability instead follows the MAJORITY (`attack` has the smaller natural mask), and NC shows NO clean differential blind spot (flags both targets ~0.60). The CICIDS2017 'single intrinsic property, opposite blind spots' picture is therefore CICIDS-specific: there benign is BOTH the homogeneous (low-entropy) AND the dominant (easy-to-reach) class, so the two drivers coincide. When they are separated (UNSW: normal is homogeneous but minority; attack is heterogeneous but majority), the unified picture partially breaks \u2014 the STRIP side generalizes (intrinsic), the NC side is frequency-linked."
  },
